// Signing defaults for every target. Simulator builds need no signing, so it is off by default
// and a fresh clone builds without an Apple developer team.
//
// To run on a device, or to build from the Xcode window with signing, copy
// Config/Local.xcconfig.example to Config/Local.xcconfig (git-ignored) and put your team ID in it.
// scripts/device.sh passes the same settings on the command line and needs no local file.
CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED = NO
CODE_SIGNING_REQUIRED = NO

// Backup integrations that need an account are off unless Config/Local.xcconfig turns them on
// (see Config/Local.xcconfig.example). Empty means off: the app leaves the destination out.
// Backing up to iCloud Drive, Google Drive or other storage that Files shows needs none of
// this: the reader picks a folder there with the system's picker.
// - TACTILE_ENTITLEMENTS: the app target's entitlements file. Empty: none, which is what an
//   unsigned simulator build and a free Personal Team need. The committed
//   Config/SignInWithApple.entitlements holds only the Sign in with Apple entitlement, for
//   Tactile Texts Cloud; set it together with SIGN_IN_WITH_APPLE = YES.
// - SIGN_IN_WITH_APPLE: YES when the build carries that entitlement; the Tactile Texts Cloud page
//   then offers Sign in with Apple. Empty: no Apple button.
// - GOOGLE_SIGNIN_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_SIGNIN_URL_SCHEME: Sign in with Google for Tactile Texts
//   Cloud (identity only, scopes openid and email). The iOS OAuth client ID from Google Cloud
//   (<digits>-<id>.apps.googleusercontent.com) and its reversed form
//   (com.googleusercontent.apps.<digits>-<id>), the redirect's URL scheme. Not secrets.
//   Empty: no Google button. With neither sign-in set, Tactile Texts Cloud says it isn't
//   available.
// - BACKUP_SERVICE_DEV_SIGNIN: development only, optional. The `dev` Worker's
//   DEV_TEST_SIGNIN_SECRET: both sign-in buttons then sign in through the Worker's test issuer,
//   so the simulator can sign in to the `dev` deployment. Debug builds only read it, and it is
//   readable in the built app: never set it for a build that leaves the developer's hands.
// - BACKUP_SERVICE_DEV_USER: development only, optional, with BACKUP_SERVICE_DEV_SIGNIN. The
//   named test user dev sign-in signs in as (empty: "dev"). The same name on every build and
//   simulator is the same account; the signed-out Tactile Texts Cloud page can change it.
// - scripts/dev-cloud.sh writes BACKUP_SERVICE_HOST, BACKUP_PRODUCT_IDS and the three
//   development settings into Config/Local.xcconfig for a local `wrangler dev`, Debug only,
//   between marked lines (`scripts/dev-cloud.sh --remove` takes them out again).
// - S3_BACKUP_*: an S3-compatible bucket (Amazon S3, Cloudflare R2, MinIO) as a backup
//   destination. Host, region, bucket and both keys must all be set for it to appear.
//   The keys end up in the built app's Info.plist, where anyone holding the app can read them:
//   use a token limited to object read and write on this one bucket, and never distribute a
//   build configured this way. Never put these values in this file; it is committed.
// - BACKUP_SERVICE_HOST and BACKUP_PRODUCT_IDS: the Tactile Texts cloud backup service (the
//   Worker's host, without a scheme) and its App Store subscription product IDs, comma-separated.
//   Not secrets. Both must be set for the service to appear; empty leaves it out of the app.
// - BACKUP_SERVICE_ATTEST_BYPASS: development only, optional. The `dev` Worker's
//   APP_ATTEST_BYPASS_SECRET, which lets the simulator (no App Attest) use the service. Debug
//   builds only read it, and it is readable in the built app: never set it for a build that
//   talks to the production Worker or leaves the developer's hands. Empty: no bypass.
// - BACKUP_TERMS_URL and BACKUP_PRIVACY_URL: the Terms of Use and Privacy Policy pages the
//   Tactile Texts Cloud offer links to, written without "https://" ("//" starts a comment in
//   this file; the app adds https). Not secrets. Empty: that link is not shown.
TACTILE_ENTITLEMENTS =
S3_BACKUP_HOST =
S3_BACKUP_REGION =
S3_BACKUP_BUCKET =
S3_BACKUP_ACCESS_KEY_ID =
S3_BACKUP_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY =
S3_BACKUP_PREFIX =
S3_BACKUP_NAME =
BACKUP_SERVICE_HOST =
BACKUP_PRODUCT_IDS =
BACKUP_SERVICE_ATTEST_BYPASS =
BACKUP_SERVICE_DEV_SIGNIN =
BACKUP_SERVICE_DEV_USER =
SIGN_IN_WITH_APPLE =
GOOGLE_SIGNIN_CLIENT_ID =
GOOGLE_SIGNIN_URL_SCHEME =
BACKUP_TERMS_URL =
BACKUP_PRIVACY_URL =

#include? "Local.xcconfig"
